   <narrative xml:lang="SV">IBFAN-Asia Pacific Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">International Baby Food Action Network (IBFAN) Asia Pacific aims to contribute to reduction in malnutrition and improvement in infant and young child survival, health and development through improvement in infant feeding practices. The broad objective of their Strategic Plan 2003-2007 is to build IBFAN&#xB4;s capacity of NGOs and civil society organizations (CSOs) to assist the governments, local authorities and</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">communities to implement the global instruments related to infant and young child feeding and build pressure on the governments to fully implement these policies to make them effective tools to improve infant andyoung child feeding. Main activities regards development, promotion and use of the Global Strategy on Infant and Young Child Feeding (GSIYCF), strengthening network and coordination, Asia Pacifi</narrative>
  </description>
